{"ref":"BDB, בִּקְעָה","hw":"בִּקְעָה","html":"† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">בִּקְעָה</span></big>  <strong>n.f. valley</strong> (cleft), <strong>plain</strong>—abs. <span dir=\"rtl\">ב׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Genesis 11:2\" href=\"/Genesis.11.2\">Gn 11:2</a> + 8 times; cstr. <span dir=\"rtl\">בִּקְעַת</span> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 34:3\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.34.3\">Dt 34:3</a> + 7 times; pl. <span dir=\"rtl\">בְּקָעוֹת</span> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 41:18\" href=\"/Isaiah.41.18\">Is 41:18</a> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 104:8\" href=\"/Psalms.104.8\">ψ 104:8</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">בְּקָעֹת</span> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 11:11\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.11.11\">Dt 11:11</a>;—<br><strong>1.</strong>  <em>valley</em> (opp. <span dir=\"rtl\">הַר</span> mountain) <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 8:7\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.8.7\">Dt 8:7</a> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 11:11\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.11.11\">11:11</a> cf. <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 41:18\" href=\"/Isaiah.41.18\">Is 41:18</a>; also <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 63:14\" href=\"/Isaiah.63.14\">63:14</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">כַּבְּהֵמָה בַּבִּקְעָה תֵרֵד</span> in creation-poem <a data-ref=\"Psalms 104:8\" href=\"/Psalms.104.8\">ψ 104:8</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">יַעֲלוּ הָרִים יֵרֽדוּ בְקָעוֹת</span>.<br><strong>2.</strong>  <em>plain</em> (sometimes valley-plain, broad valley) <a data-ref=\"Genesis 11:2\" href=\"/Genesis.11.2\">Gn 11:2</a>; also <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 3:22\" href=\"/Ezekiel.3.22\">Ez 3:22</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 3:23\" href=\"/Ezekiel.3.23\">23</a>; <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 8:4\" href=\"/Ezekiel.8.4\">8:4</a>; <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 37:1\" href=\"/Ezekiel.37.1\">37:1</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 37:2\" href=\"/Ezekiel.37.2\">2</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">(עַל־פְּנֵי הַבּ׳)</span> as level, opp. <span dir=\"rtl\">הָֽרְכָסִים</span> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 40:4\" href=\"/Isaiah.40.4\">Is 40:4</a> (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">מִישׁוֹר</span>); elsewhere cstr., mostly with n.pr. <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 34:3\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.34.3\">Dt 34:3</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">ב׳ יְרֵחוֹ</span> (appos. <span dir=\"rtl\">הַכִּכָּר</span>), <span dir=\"rtl\">ב׳ מִצְפֶּה</span> <a data-ref=\"Joshua 11:8\" href=\"/Joshua.11.8\">Jos 11:8</a>, <span dir=\"rtl\">ב׳ הַלְּבָנוֹן</span> <a data-ref=\"Joshua 11:17\" href=\"/Joshua.11.17\">11:17</a>; <a data-ref=\"Joshua 12:7\" href=\"/Joshua.12.7\">12:7</a>, <span dir=\"rtl\">ב׳ מִגִדּוֹ</span> <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 35:22\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.35.22\">2 Ch 35:22</a> cf. <a data-ref=\"Zechariah 12:11\" href=\"/Zechariah.12.11\">Zc 12:11</a>, <span dir=\"rtl\">ב׳ אוֹנוֹ</span> <a data-ref=\"Nehemiah 6:2\" href=\"/Nehemiah.6.2\">Ne 6:2</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">ב׳־אָוֶן</span> <a data-ref=\"Amos 1:5\" href=\"/Amos.1.5\">Am 1:5</a> <em>plain of idolatry</em> = Baalbek (Damascus, according to Wetzst in De<sup>Jes 3, 702</sup>; 𝔊 πέδιον Ὤν).","next":"BDB, בְּקִיעַ","prev":"BDB, בֶּ֫קַע"}